lisa-design:
- Problem code for a store that stopped writing is `store-read-only` (matches the Go sentinel store.ErrReadOnly PR 5 maps to the 503); PR 5 adds the CodeStoreReadOnly constant in internal/server/problem.go with this string.
- Writing operations = every operation whose handler writes to the store: registerAgent, updateAgent, deregisterAgent, createEnrollment, deleteEnrollment, leaseTask (a GET that commits a lease), heartbeatLease, completeLease, abandonLease, uploadTranscript, uploadEnvironmentLog, createEffect, postCommand, closeWorkItem, deleteWorkItem, authCallback (session create, UsedLoginState), logout (session delete), receiveWebhook (Delivery). replayEvent already had 503.
- Not included: login (P3 makes the OAuth state self-contained, no store write), dryRunCatalog (no side effects), reads authenticated by an agent token or a session (the token renewal and expired-session delete are best-effort, logged, never fail the read).
- /readyz keeps the shared ServiceUnavailable $ref; the conditions are in the operation's description. For memory and the file store, which have nothing to sync, "first sync" counts as done once loaded.
- api-server.md §Startup order keeps the work-item Rebuild step (PR 5 removes the code); only its "(/readyz 200)" tie to Options.Ready goes.

